# Scavenge-first

Before new modules (scrapers, matchers, charts, FX, job queues):

1. **Search** GitHub / Apify / sibling repos / known OSS for battle-tested patterns.
2. **Adapt + wrap** — prefer provider interfaces so swapped adapters don't rewrite core.
3. **Cite** source in a short code comment or `docs/ATTRIBUTIONS.md`.
4. Only build from scratch when nothing fit-for-purpose exists — note why in PR/decision log.

## Scavenge targets (Beyoracle)

- [PokeDao](https://github.com/ChicoPanama/PokeDao) — L0/L1/L2 + CardMatcher cascading match
- [tcg_mcp pricing Protocol](https://github.com/seanlok/tcg-mcp) — `PricingSource` interface pattern
- Apify Mercari sold comps actors (future live path)
- Community Beyblade DBs (beybxdb, wiki dumps) — seed only, not sole source of truth

## Provider pattern

```typescript
interface PricingSource {
  id: SourceId;
  search(query: string, opts?: SearchOpts): Promise<RawListing[]>;
  normalize(raw: RawListing): Observation;
}
```

Match oracle core stays adapter-agnostic.
